## Next Steps: Complete Resilience Testing

NEXT TASK 9.4: Write resilience and error handling tests

This is the final task in the resilience module. It will validate all the error handling,
recovery, and resilience mechanisms implemented in Tasks 9.1-9.3.

Requirements:
- Test circuit breaker behavior under various failure scenarios
  * Test state transitions (closed → open → half-open → closed)
  * Test failure threshold triggering
  * Test recovery timeout and half-open state
  * Test concurrent requests during state transitions
  
- Test retry logic and timeout handling
  * Test exponential backoff with jitter
  * Test maximum retry limits
  * Test timeout handling and cancellation
  * Test retry with different error types
  
- Test error propagation and logging
  * Test error tracking and aggregation
  * Test error rate calculation
  * Test structured logging with context
  * Test distributed tracing correlation
  
- Test recovery mechanisms and system stability
